{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"supersweet-knavish-nymph","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The SIDECAR channel records gate-run limits but not gate-run consumption\n\nDiscovered by the Step-7 sibling sweep while fixing [rebar:aec1-76e7-bb95-4c86]. `aec1` fixed the\n**usage-log** channel (`.rebar/usage.jsonl`). The **sidecar** channel — the one an operator reaches\nwith `rebar audit show <ticket>`, and the one that lives in the store — still has the same defect in\nthree places.\n\n## 1. The sanitization allowlist admits the ceiling and drops the measurement\n\n`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:82-96` — `_ALLOWED_FIELDS` contains `request_limit` and\n`tool_calls_limit` but **not** `requests` or `tool_calls`. So a gate error durably records *what the\nlimit was* and never *what was consumed*, which is precisely the half that makes the record\nactionable. Identical construct to aec1's root cause: a fixed allowlist that admits the ceiling and\ndiscards the measurement.\n\nBoth candidate fields are plain integers carrying no prompt, response or argument content, so this\nis safe on the privacy contract — but `_ALLOWED_FIELDS` is a **sanitization boundary**, and widening\nit is a privacy decision that deserves its own review rather than riding in on a telemetry fix.\nThat is why aec1 filed this instead of folding it in.\n\n## 2. Five of six `emit_gate_error` call sites pass no diagnostic at all\n\n`workflow/gate_dispatch.py:122, 180, 351, 467, 518` are all `cause=`-only. Only\n`workflow/completion_recovery.py:388-395` passes a `diagnostic=`, and that is the completion\n**bounded-recovery** arm alone (it seeds and allowlists `requests`/`tool_calls`/`tool_calls_limit`\nat `:255-267`, which is why that one arm works). A plan-review gate error, or a completion\n*preflight* gate error, therefore persists no counters whatsoever.\n\n## 3. The completion verdict sidecar carries no run metadata at all\n\n`completion_sidecar.py:271-306` — the payload is verdict/criteria/findings/remediation/runner/model/\n`verified_at_sha`/`trace_id`/`material_fingerprint`/`certifiable`. No requests, no tool calls, no\nduration. By contrast the plan-review sidecar already carries per-call `requests`\n(`plan_review/sizing.py:292-310`) and a `metrics` block with `det_ms`/`llm_ms`/`total_ms`/\n`llm_calls` (`workflow/plan_review_recovery.py:151-177`) — so the two gates are **asymmetric**, and\nthe completion gate (the one whose step budget was raised five times) is the blind one.\n\n## Why this matters after aec1\n\naec1 makes the numbers exist on disk in `.rebar/usage.jsonl`, which is per-checkout and not shared.\nThe sidecar channel is the one that rides the ticket store and is therefore visible to every agent\nand every later reader. Until this is closed, \"how much did this ticket's gates cost\" is answerable\nlocally but still not answerable **from the store** — the exact phrasing of the original complaint.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `requests` and `tool_calls` are admitted by `failure.py:_ALLOWED_FIELDS`, with the privacy\n      rationale recorded next to them (integers only, no content)\n- [ ] every `emit_gate_error` call site passes a diagnostic carrying the consumed counters, or the\n      ticket records per-site why a given site legitimately has none\n- [ ] the completion verdict sidecar carries requests/tool_calls/duration, reaching parity with the\n      plan-review sidecar's existing `metrics` block\n- [ ] a test proves the counters survive to the SIDECAR for a FAILING gate run, not only a passing\n      one (the axis aec1 established must vary here too)\n- [ ] `rebar audit show <ticket>` surfaces them","id":"df94-66ba-dbf8-4ac1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"The sidecar channel records gate-run limits but not gate-run consumption"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785950887264908001,"uuid":"c88590e0-3d98-40d0-a61d-2fcdd3ba70fe"}